s after t=43165 (step_08), and its in-window 2-hop neighborhood is empty (step_05). No time-respecting path to 361 exists under the 600-unit gap constraint (step_01) or even with unlimited waiting (step_04), and path enumeration returns nothing (step_14). Confounders were tested and rejected: a static time-ignoring connection does exist via shared hubs 28/399/669/724/810 (step_12) and an unconstrained temporal route reaches 361 (step_11), but it starts at t=43474 outside the window with hop waits up to 36136, far exceeding 600. Abundant ambient activity (5150 events, step_02) and 361's own in-window activity with 4 partners (step_07) do not create a path. Extending to the full or post-window range still fails, reaching only 6 nodes (step_09, step_15). Conclusion: absent, since the source is provably inactive in the queried interval rather than merely under-observed."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**No cascade exists.** The decisive fact: **node 1330 has zero events in [4765, 43165]** (step_03, step_06). All 7 of its interactions occur *after* t=43165 (step_08). A cascade cannot originate from a node that never acts within the window \u2014 the 2-hop neighborhood of 1330 in-window is literally empty (step_05).\n\nI ruled out each of the three warned-against confounders:\n\n- **Static connectivity:** 1330 and 361 *are* connected when time is ignored \u2014 step_12 shows a dense shared neighborhood (hubs 28, 399, 669, 724, 810). This is the trap, and it is not evidence of a cascade.\n- **Unconstrained temporal route:** step_11 finds a 7-hop route reaching 361, but it begins at t=43474 (outside the window) and requires hop waits of 1368\u201336136 units \u2014 60\u00d7 the 600-unit limit. Relaxing max_wait entirely still fails inside the window (step_04).\n- **Activity volume:** the graph holds 5150 events over 1901 nodes in-window (step_02), and 361 is genuinely active with 4 partners (step_07). Ample surrounding traffic produces no valid path \u2014 step_14 enumerates zero paths.\n\nEven extending to the full timeline or the post-window period, the 600-unit constraint caps propagation at 6 nodes and never reaches 361 (step_09, step_15). This is a firm **absent**, not \"insufficient\": the data is complete and unambiguously negative.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_dc3dfaa5\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1330, 361],\n  \"window\": [4765, 43165],\n  \"confidence\": 0.96,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 1330 records zero interactions inside [4765,43165] (step_03, step_06); its entire 7-event history falls after t=43165 (step_08), and its in-window 2-hop neighborhood is empty (step_05). No time-respecting path to 361 exists under the 600-unit gap constraint (step_01) or even with unlimited waiting (step_04), and path enumeration returns nothing (step_14). Confounders were tested and rejected: a static time-ignoring connection does exist via shared hubs 28/399/669/724/810 (step_12) and an unconstrained temporal route reaches 361 (step_11), but it starts at t=43474 outside the window with hop waits up to 36136, far exceeding 600. Abundant ambient activity (5150 events, step_02) and 361's own in-window activity with 4 partners (step_07) do not create a path. Extending to the full or post-window range still fails, reaching only 6 nodes (step_09, step_15). Conclusion: absent, since the source is provably inactive in the queried interval rather than merely under-observed.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 53187, "total_output_tokens": 3820, "total_tokens": 57007, "total_latency_ms": 62035, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}